==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Commando Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Cameraman Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
Prior to True Form, Mer-Cat fails to properly serve her purpose, as many [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating Enemies]] are powerful melee pushers, and she cannot outrange them, not to mention her single target. She can still shine in certain stages such as [[Attack on W-Cyclone (Expert)|Attack on W-Cyclone]] due to her high damage, though it is wise to get her [[True Form]] as soon as possible.

==='''True Form'''===
With area attacks, higher health and much better range, Cameraman Cat becomes an extremely efficient DPS unit against Floating enemies. A big enough stack of them will reduce even the mighty [[Teacher Bun Bun]] and most of his variants to rubble, as well as many short-ranged floating enemies like [[Shy Boy]]. Her overall great stats, outside of speed, make her an excellent, low investment midrange attacker for all sorts of grounded enemies too. With proper meatshielding, she can be extremely useful in stages such as [[Head Shaker (Insane)|Head Shaker]], [[Tiny Horns (Deadly)|Tiny Horns]] and [[Lots O' Lion (Deadly)|Lots O' Lion]] as she can quickly accumulate DPS and these single target enemies often have trouble breaking through a huge stack of them if they ever get past your meatshields.

Cameraman can also work great as a ranged meatshield against [[Dolphina]] or [[:Category:Wave Attack Enemies|Wave Attackers]] like [[Dober P.D]]; she will stack up damage while either staying in a blindspot or far enough from the enemy to not give them the chance to attack and release the waves often.

Research UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]] like [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]] and [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]] can be used to make Cameraman Cat even more spammable than she already is, sometimes resulting in an impassable wall of strong attacks. Keep in mind, however, that she will drain money faster, especially if you use a CPU.

==='''Talents'''===
Since Cameraman relies on both offense and defense, the Attack Buff, Health Buff and Survive talents directly contribute in making this unit much better; boost her with + levels and catseyes as well though, for these talents will not do much on their own.

Cameraman's [[Critical Hit]] is also fairly cheap and allows for very strong hits being landed on [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal enemies]] every once in a while, although due to the mere 2% chance, it is not clever to rely on her as your only anti-metal. If you know what to expect from a stage, bring another crit. hitter, a combo to increase crit chance or something to stall the metal army enough for crits to reliably come out.

Wave Resistance can allow a stack of Cameramen to tank stray waves much better, making them especially powerful against [[Pigeon de Sable]] and [[Bore Jr.|Bore Jr]]. Waves are normally dangerous for a slow unit who relies on stacking in great numbers, so cutting their damage is highly beneficial.

==='''Orb'''===
Such a multi-purpose unit would benefit from any attack or defense up orb to a degree, but it's recommended for you to improve her effectiveness with a Floating Strong Up Orb. Alternatively, she can become Wave Immune by equipping an S-tier Wave Resist Orb if her Wave Resist talent is maxed. As generalist unit, Mer-cat would benefit from the Dodge Orb with her Survive ability, but a Strong Up Orb is still the preferred choice to better improve targeted matchups.

